course: dictionary
lesson: 3189
title: One word, many meanings: end
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word end can mean different things, and the sentence tells you which one. «The end of the story was a happy one.» Here end is the last part of the story. «Pair the numbers from both ends to add fast» uses end to mean the far tip or edge of a row.
explain: End can also be a doing word. «The Ottoman sultan Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453, ending the Byzantine Empire.» Ending means stopping or finishing. Ask yourself: is end a thing, a place, or an action? That question will often settle the meaning.
explain: Some phrases with end have a meaning that is not just the words added together. «In the end» means finally, after everything else. When you meet a phrase, read the whole thing, then check that your meaning fits the sentence.
fact: End means the last part of something, such as the end of a story or the end of a day.
fact: An end is also the far tip or edge of something long, like the end of a rope or a road.
fact: To end means to stop or to finish.
fact: An end can also mean an aim, which is what you want to get.
fact: «In the end» means finally, and «end up» means to finish in a place or state.
exercise: «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end.» In this sentence, what does end mean? | The last part of a story | An aim | *The far tip or edge of something | To stop or finish
exercise: «To find how many there were at the start, begin at the end and undo each step.» What does end mean here? | The far tip of a rope | To stop a game | *The last step or point | An aim you want to reach
exercise: «The Ottoman sultan Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453, ending the Byzantine Empire.» What does ending mean? | Starting something new | *Stopping or finishing | Winning a prize | Keeping safe
test: «We swam at the deep end of the pool.» Which meaning of end is this? | *The far part or tip of something long | An aim | The last part of a day | To stop or finish
test: Dad says «In the end, we got there.» What does in the end mean? | Without any help | *Finally, after everything else | At the start of the trip | Very quickly
exam: Which sentence uses end as a verb meaning to stop? | «She was at the end of the queue.» | «The rope has a frayed end.» | *«The bell will end the game at noon.» | «The story has a happy end.»
